.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_GET_EXTENSION_FLAGS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_get0_subject_key_id ,
.Nm X509_get0_authority_key_id ,
.Nm X509_get0_authority_issuer ,
.Nm X509_get0_authority_serial ,
.Nm X509_get_pathlen ,
.Nm X509_get_extension_flags ,
.Nm X509_get_key_usage ,
.Nm X509_get_extended_key_usage ,
.Nm X509_set_proxy_flag ,
.Nm X509_set_proxy_pathlen ,
.Nm X509_get_proxy_pathlen
.Nd retrieve certificate extension data
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509v3.h
.Ft long
.Fo X509_get_pathlen
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft uint32_t
.Fo X509_get_extension_flags
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft uint32_t
.Fo X509_get_key_usage
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft uint32_t
.Fo X509_get_extended_key_usage
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_OCTET_STRING *
.Fo X509_get0_subject_key_id
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_OCTET_STRING *
.Fo X509_get0_authority_key_id
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const GENERAL_NAMES *
.Fo X509_get0_authority_issuer
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_INTEGER *
.Fo X509_get0_authority_serial
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo X509_set_proxy_flag
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo X509_set_proxy_pathlen
.Fa "int l"
.Fc
.Ft long
.Fo X509_get_proxy_pathlen
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions retrieve information related to commonly used
certificate extensions.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_pathlen
retrieves the path length extension from a certificate.
This extension is used to limit the length of a cert chain that may be
issued from that CA.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_extension_flags
retrieves general information about a certificate, it will return one or
more of the following flags ored together.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy EXFLAG_V1
The certificate is an obsolete version 1 certificate.
.It Sy EXFLAG_BCONS
The certificate contains a basic constraints extension.
.It Sy EXFLAG_CA
The certificate contains basic constraints and asserts the CA flag.
.It Sy EXFLAG_PROXY
The certificate is a valid proxy certificate.
.It Sy EXFLAG_SI
The certificate is self issued (that is subject and issuer names match).
.It Sy EXFLAG_SS
The subject and issuer names match and extension values imply it is self
signed.
.It Sy EXFLAG_FRESHEST
The freshest CRL extension is present in the certificate.
.It Sy EXFLAG_CRITICAL
The certificate contains an unhandled critical extension.
.It Sy EXFLAG_INVALID
Some certificate extension values are invalid or inconsistent.
The certificate should be rejected.
This bit may also be raised after an out-of-memory error while
processing the X509 object, so it may not be related to the processed
ASN1 object itself.
.It Sy EXFLAG_NO_FINGERPRINT
Failed to compute the internal SHA1 hash value of the certificate or
CRL. This may be due to malloc failure or because no SHA1 implementation
was found.
.It Sy EXFLAG_INVALID_POLICY
The NID_certificate_policies certificate extension is invalid or
inconsistent.
The certificate should be rejected.
This bit may also be raised after an out-of-memory error while
processing the X509 object, so it may not be related to the processed
ASN1 object itself.
.It Sy EXFLAG_KUSAGE
The certificate contains a key usage extension.
The value can be retrieved using
.Fn X509_get_key_usage .
.It Sy EXFLAG_XKUSAGE
The certificate contains an extended key usage extension.
The value can be retrieved using
.Fn X509_get_extended_key_usage .
.El
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_key_usage
returns the value of the key usage extension.
If key usage is present will return zero or more of the flags:
.Sy KU_DIGITAL_SIGNATURE ,
.Sy KU_NON_REPUDIATION ,
.Sy KU_KEY_ENCIPHERMENT ,
.Sy KU_DATA_ENCIPHERMENT ,
.Sy KU_KEY_AGREEMENT ,
.Sy KU_KEY_CERT_SIGN ,
.Sy KU_CRL_SIGN ,
.Sy KU_ENCIPHER_ONLY
or
.Sy KU_DECIPHER_ONLY
corresponding to individual key usage bits.
If key usage is absent then
.Sy UINT32_MAX
is returned.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_extended_key_usage
returns the value of the extended key usage extension.
If extended key usage is present it will return zero or more of the
flags:
.Sy XKU_SSL_SERVER ,
.Sy XKU_SSL_CLIENT ,
.Sy XKU_SMIME ,
.Sy XKU_CODE_SIGN
.Sy XKU_OCSP_SIGN ,
.Sy XKU_TIMESTAMP ,
.Sy XKU_DVCS
or
.Sy XKU_ANYEKU .
These correspond to the OIDs
.Sy id-kp-serverAuth ,
.Sy id-kp-clientAuth ,
.Sy id-kp-emailProtection ,
.Sy id-kp-codeSigning ,
.Sy id-kp-OCSPSigning ,
.Sy id-kp-timeStamping ,
.Sy id-kp-dvcs
and
.Sy anyExtendedKeyUsage
respectively.
Additionally
.Sy XKU_SGC
is set if either Netscape or Microsoft SGC OIDs are present.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_subject_key_id
returns an internal pointer to the subject key identifier of
.Fa x
as an
.Sy ASN1_OCTET_STRING
or
.Dv NULL
if the extension is not present or cannot be parsed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_authority_key_id
returns an internal pointer to the authority key identifier of
.Fa x
as an
.Sy ASN1_OCTET_STRING
or
.Dv NULL
if the extension is not present or cannot be parsed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_authority_issuer
returns an internal pointer to the authority certificate issuer of
.Fa x
as a stack of
.Sy GENERAL_NAME
structures or
.Dv NULL
if the extension is not present or cannot be parsed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_authority_serial
returns an internal pointer to the authority certificate serial number
of
.Fa x
as an
.Sy ASN1_INTEGER
or
.Dv NULL
if the extension is not present or cannot be parsed.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set_proxy_flag
marks the certificate with the
.Sy EXFLAG_PROXY
flag.
This is for the users who need to mark non-RFC3820 proxy certificates as
such, as OpenSSL only detects RFC3820 compliant ones.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set_proxy_pathlen
sets the proxy certificate path length for the given certificate
.Fa x .
This is for the users who need to mark non-RFC3820 proxy certificates as
such, as OpenSSL only detects RFC3820 compliant ones.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_proxy_pathlen
returns the proxy certificate path length for the given certificate
.Fa x
if it is a proxy certificate.
.Sh NOTES
The value of the flags correspond to extension values which are cached
in the
.Vt X509
structure.
If the flags returned do not provide sufficient information an
application should examine extension values directly for example using
.Xr X509_get_ext_d2i 3 .
.Pp
If the key usage or extended key usage extension is absent then
typically usage is unrestricted.
For this reason
.Fn X509_get_key_usage
and
.Fn X509_get_extended_key_usage
return
.Sy UINT32_MAX
when the corresponding extension is absent.
Applications can additionally check the return value of
.Fn X509_get_extension_flags
and take appropriate action is an extension is absent.
.Pp
If
.Fn X509_get0_subject_key_id
returns
.Dv NULL
then the extension may be absent or malformed.
Applications can determine the precise reason using
.Xr X509_get_ext_d2i 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_get_pathlen
returns the path length value, or -1 if the extension is not present.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_extension_flags ,
.Fn X509_get_key_usage
and
.Fn X509_get_extended_key_usage
return sets of flags corresponding to the certificate extension values.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_subject_key_id
returns the subject key identifier as a pointer to an
.Sy ASN1_OCTET_STRING
structure or
.Dv NULL
if the extension is absent or an error occurred during parsing.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_proxy_pathlen
returns the path length value if the given certificate is a proxy one
and has a path length set, and -1 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr X509_check_purpose 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn X509_get_pathlen ,
.Fn X509_set_proxy_flag ,
.Fn X509_set_proxy_pathlen
and
.Fn X509_get_proxy_pathlen
were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
